7
00:00:19.159 --> 00:00:20.673
B1, then B4.

8
00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:38.980
What you get: a complete design for a multi-hospital chain in India (10 hospitals, 3,000 beds, 30 clinics, telemedicine), explained the way it actually runs: how a patient moves through registration, OPD, emergency, admission, surgery, discharge and billing,

9
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:52.188
and what each system does at every step;. the clinical record (EHR) and how orders, results, medications and notes flow;. lab, radiology (PACS), pharmacy, nursing, operating theatres and beds;.

10
00:00:53.538 --> 00:01:00.514
insurance and cashless claims;. telemedicine video consultations and e-prescriptions;. interoperability:

11
00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:21.402
HL7 v2, FHIR, DICOM, and India's Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM);. the algorithms behind patient matching, scheduling, bed assignment, early-warning scores, drug checks, inventory and claims;. the data platform: operational stores, event streaming, data lake, warehouse, research data model and ML;.

12
00:01:22.752 --> 00:01:29.835
the tech stack, layer by layer;. security, privacy, consent, compliance, reliability and disaster recovery.

13
